l leader =E2=80=94 outside of Beijing and Moscow =E2=80=94 has voiced. The =
world, he said, should lift or ease harsh economic sanctions on North Korea=
 in exchange for halting its nuclear weapons program.</span></p><p style=3D=
"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>=E2=
=80=8BThe idea challenges decades of official U.S. policy, which relies on =
squeezing Pyongyang until it gives up its nukes. Still, Lee pitched this st=
rategy directly to President Trump, who is looking to restart personal dipl=
omacy with the North Korean leader, Kim Jong-un.</span></p><p style=3D"font=
:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Lee=E2=80=
=99s core argument was simple: What other realistic option does the U.S. ac=
tually have=3F</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;co=
lor:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Consider the facts on the ground.</span></p=
><div style=3D"margin:0 auto;max-width:600px;width:100%"><table><tbody><tr>=
