SWi-U6EA38XDgEqNr_RDJv50Xi7V94msk7KFS1d-_RK" class=3D"css-sdwaa1" style=3D"=
color:#286ed0;-webkit-text-decoration:underline;text-decoration:underline">=
collapsed</a><span> =E2=80=8Bover the question of timing. Pyongyang wanted =
early sanctions relief, while the U.S. was unwilling to give up its stronge=
st leverage.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;colo=
r:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Kim returned home frustrated. But a strategic=
 opening emerged with the war in Ukraine. Pyongyang supplied troops and wea=
pons to Russia; Russia strengthened its economic and military ties with Nor=
th Korea. China, wary of losing influence in Pyongyang, expanded its own tr=
